/-
# Edge flattenings and phylogenetic invariants of the general Markov model

In the `κ`-state general Markov model on a tree `T` rooted at a vertex `r`, a root distribution
`π` and a Markov matrix on every edge directed away from `r` give the joint distribution of the
states at all vertices, `π(σ(r)) ∏_{a → b} M_{ab}(σ(a), σ(b))`, and hence the joint distribution
`P` of the leaf states, the sum over the states at the other vertices (`leafDist`). Allman and
Rhodes (2008, Section 2) write `φ_r` for this parameterization; the affine phylogenetic variety is
the closure of its image, independent of `r`, and the phylogenetic ideal `𝔞_T` is the homogeneous
ideal of the corresponding projective variety, that is, the ideal of polynomials vanishing on all
scalar multiples of distributions in the image (`phylogeneticIdeal`, over `ℂ`).

An edge `e` of `T` induces a split `A | B` of the taxa; the flattening `Flat_e(P)` is the
`κ^|A| × κ^|B|` matrix with entries `P(u, v)` (`flatten`). Since
`Flat_e(P) = M₁ᵀ diag(π_r) M₂` for `κ`-row Markov matrices `M₁, M₂`, it has rank at most `κ`, and
its `(κ + 1) × (κ + 1)` minors are phylogenetic invariants (edge invariants). Theorem 4: for
`κ = 2` and every binary tree, `𝔞_T` is generated by the `3 × 3` minors of all edge flattenings
of a tensor of indeterminates. For four taxa, a flattening along a split that is not an edge of
the tree has rank larger than `κ` outside a proper algebraic subset of the parameter space
(Allman and Rhodes 2006, Theorem 2 with `λ = κ`); since the parameter space is an affine space and
the locus where all `(κ + 1)`-minors vanish is algebraic, that subset is proper exactly when one
parameter value gives rank larger than `κ`, the form in which
`exists_card_lt_rank_flatten_nonEdge` states it.

Trees are the repository's unrooted binary phylogenetic trees (`UnrootedBinaryTree`) with their
edge splits and quartets (`CSLibExt.Bioinformatics.Phylogenetics.Splits`); the root may be any
vertex.

Sources: E. S. Allman and J. A. Rhodes, "Phylogenetic ideals and varieties for the general Markov
model", Advances in Applied Mathematics 40 (2008) 127–148, doi:10.1016/j.aam.2006.10.002,
Section 2 and Theorem 4; E. S. Allman and J. A. Rhodes, "The identifiability of tree topology for
phylogenetic models, including covarion and mixture models", Journal of Computational Biology 13
(2006) 1101–1113, doi:10.1089/cmb.2006.13.1101, Theorem 2.
-/
module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import CSLibExt.Bioinformatics.Phylogenetics.Splits
public import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Rank
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Basic
public import CSLibExt.Biology.ComputationalBiology.GeneralMarkovFlattening

@[expose] public section

namespace WantedExt.Biology.ComputationalBiology.GeneralMarkovFlatteningWanted

open MathlibExt.Biology.Phylogenetics.UnrootedTreeCount
open Cslib.Bioinformatics.Phylogenetics.Splits

variable {X : Type} [Fintype X] [DecidableEq X]

/-- The **phylogenetic ideal** `𝔞_T` of the two-state general Markov model on `T`: the
polynomials in the indeterminates `p_u`, `u : X → Fin 2`, that vanish at every scalar multiple of
every leaf distribution `φ_r(π, M)` with complex stochastic parameters, for every root `r`. -/
def phylogeneticIdeal (T : UnrootedBinaryTree X) : Ideal (MvPolynomial (X → Fin 2) ℂ) where
  carrier := {f | ∀ (r : T.V) (π : Fin 2 → ℂ) (M : T.V → T.V → Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ),
    IsComplexStochastic T.G r π M → ∀ c : ℂ,
      MvPolynomial.eval (fun u => c * leafDist T.G (leafOf T) r π M u) f = 0}
  add_mem' := by
    intro f g hf hg r π M hp c
    simp [hf r π M hp c, hg r π M hp c]
  zero_mem' := by
    intro r π M hp c
    simp
  smul_mem' := by
    intro a f hf r π M hp c
    simp [hf r π M hp c]

/-- The **edge invariants** for two states: the `3 × 3` minors of the flattenings, along all edge
splits of `T`, of the tensor of indeterminates `(p_u)_{u : X → Fin 2}`. -/
def edgeMinors (T : UnrootedBinaryTree X) : Set (MvPolynomial (X → Fin 2) ℂ) :=
  {f | ∃ A ∈ edgeSplits T, ∃ (rows : Fin 3 → ({x // x ∈ A} → Fin 2))
    (cols : Fin 3 → ({x // x ∉ A} → Fin 2)),
      f = ((flatten A (fun u => MvPolynomial.X u)).submatrix rows cols).det}

/-- **The phylogenetic ideal is generated by the edge invariants** (Allman and Rhodes 2008,
Theorem 4): for `κ = 2` and any number of taxa, the phylogenetic ideal of the general Markov
model on an unrooted binary phylogenetic tree `T` is generated by the `3 × 3` minors of all edge
flattenings of a `2 × ⋯ × 2` tensor of indeterminates.

Source: Allman and Rhodes (2008), Theorem 4. -/
public theorem_wanted phylogeneticIdeal_eq_span_edgeMinors (T : UnrootedBinaryTree X) :
    phylogeneticIdeal T = Ideal.span (edgeMinors T)

end WantedExt.Biology.ComputationalBiology.GeneralMarkovFlatteningWanted
